# Intent: Four fixes to the first run that a parent would trip over (found by reading the flow as a person who has never seen the robot, docs/design/first-run-flow.md). (1) A small Skip at the top right of the language and name steps and of the brain step: the robot still works with the defaults (English, StackChan, and the brain default below) and everything stays changeable on the settings page. (2) Step 1 no longer says "Pick your language" in English only: the title is "Hello, Hola, Bonjour, Hallo, Ola, Ciao" and the six tiles are each language's own name, English highlighted. (3) "How should I think?" becomes "Where should my brain live?" with the three ways of owner decision 12 of 2026-11-18: MaiPai Home, My own servers, Set one up for me (translated in all six languages). The core takes mode 2 = set one up for me (0 home, 1 own servers); the default shown is Home when a hub is already known, else set one up for me; Skip takes the shown answer. The answer is saved and sent as before; the host builds the three ways (docs/plan/first-run-brain-choice.md), nothing on the robot changes behavior on it. (4) After All set! a last screen says what to do next: say Hi, Stack Chan; change anything on the settings page, with its address (the host the unit talks to, port 8051, from the saved websocket address, or a plain sentence when the unit has none); the phone code on that page. The answers are saved when All set! shows, so a person who walks away at the last screen keeps them; the last screen closes on its button or after two minutes. No QR code: the LVGL QR widget is not built into this firmware and costs memory; the settings page shows the phone code as a QR.
# Placement: unit (the first run runs on the robot with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_firstrun.cc, maipai_firstrun.h, maipai_firstrun_core.h and maipai_firstrun_wire.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: wipe the first-run record and run the flow: Skip on the language and name steps keeps English and StackChan; the brain step has three answers and "Set one up for me" is highlighted with no hub known; after All set! the last screen shows the settings address of your host and its button closes it; first_run_done carries mode 2 when "Set one up for me" was chosen.
# Kconfig: none

